# The a is further open than Castilian's, which is the only edit in this file
# that is not IBM's. It was 660 and 1400 and it is 700 and 1350: Catalan's a
# is the open central vowel and Castilian's sat close enough to our schwa --
# 600 and 1500 then -- that casa's two vowels were hard to tell apart. The
# schwa moved in at the same time and ss_ssval.up says the rest of it. The
# third formant is Castilian's still, and so is every context test below.
#
# A lift of ss_ssval.obj for caes would put Castilian's numbers back.
